[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113346,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Myoepithelioma (ME) is a benign salivary gland neoplasm that is composed almost exclusively of myoepithelial cells and the stroma they produce.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113347,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8982/0 Myoepithelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113348,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.1 &amp; XH3CQ8 Benign neoplasm of other specified major salivary glands &amp; Myoepithelioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113349,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> myoepithelial cell tumour; myoepithelial adenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113350,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113351,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most MEs occur in the parotid gland, followed by the palate; less commonly, they occur in submandibular gland {33231965}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113352,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour usually presents as a painless slow-growing mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113353,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>ME accounts for 1.5% of all salivary gland tumours. It constitutes 2.2% and 5.7% of major and minor salivary gland tumours, respectively. The patient age range is 9&ndash;85&nbsp;years (mean: 44&nbsp;years), and it affects both sexes equally {1325089; 2423468; 2982059; 6277451; 7557900; 8734420; 11269218}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113354,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113355,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A few cases show <em>EWSR1</em> rearrangements, with no correlation with histological patterns {28648935}. <em>NTF3</em>::<em>PLAG1</em>, <em>FBXO32</em>::<em>PLAG1</em>, and <em>GEM</em>::<em>PLAG1</em> fusions have been detected in oncocytic ME {32673681}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113356,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are solid and well-circumscribed, and they exhibit tan to yellow glistening cut surfaces.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113357,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>ME shows well-circumscribed and often encapsulated borders. The myoepithelial cells can be spindled, epithelioid, plasmacytoid, or clear, or in variable combinations thereof {25970687; 30665928}, and they may be arranged in nested, cord-like, trabeculated, or reticular patterns. The stroma can be myxoid, collagenous, or vascular. Abundant intracellular mucin is a rare reported finding {23821216; 24595421; 28614209}, and oncocytic changes may be found. Encapsulation is uncommon in the minor salivary gland tumours.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>ME is positive for keratins, S100, SOX10, and myoepithelial markers such as p63, calponin, and SMA.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The well-defined borders of the tumour and the lack of invasive growth distinguish ME from myoepithelial carcinoma {25970687; 30789358}. The characteristic basaloid biphasic pattern, peripheral palisading, and minimal to absent myxoid stroma of basal cell adenoma help to separate it from ME. Monomorphic histology and rare or absent ductal structures in ME separate it from pleomorphic adenoma {19926180; 33231965}. Distinguishing from soft tissue ME may be difficult, given the overlapping histological features and the presence of <em>PLAG1</em> gene rearrangements in both {23630011}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T12:25:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113358,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears show variable cellularity, with bland myoepithelial cells (spindled, epithelioid, clear, or plasmacytoid) as a single cell type or mixed, in loosely cohesive tissue fragments with strands of hyaline stroma or as single cells. There is no myxofibrillary stroma. Necrosis and nuclear atypia suggest myoepithelial carcinoma, but because tumour invasion cannot be assessed, it is impossible to differentiate ME from myoepithelial carcinoma on cytopathology {25970687}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113359,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of <em>PLAG1</em> rearrangement by cytogenetics or other methods can be helpful {28648935; 32673681}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113360,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> almost exclusive myoepithelial differentiation and absence of invasion.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> tumour encapsulation (except in minor salivary glands).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113361,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113362,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 64,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>ME is a benign tumour that shows a low recurrence rate. The tumour is treated by complete surgical resection. Malignant transformation to myoepithelial carcinoma has been reported but seems to be extremely rare {8882360; 10843278}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:10:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]